1
00:00:13,728 --> 00:00:17,832
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:19,734
[mortar explosions]

3
00:00:19,734 --> 00:00:21,369
Boy, I feel like an idiot.

4
00:00:21,369 --> 00:00:24,205
I'm showing up with a gun
to an artillery fight.

5
00:00:24,205 --> 00:00:28,376
That's like showing up with a rocket
launcher to a tactical warhead fight.

6
00:00:28,376 --> 00:00:31,479
Of course, I didn't KNOW this
was going to be an artillery fight.

7
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:33,414
[mortar fire]

8
00:00:33,414 --> 00:00:34,382
Oh, boy.

9
00:00:34,382 --> 00:00:35,583
[explosions]

10
00:00:35,583 --> 00:00:37,151
I don't even want to be here!

11
00:00:37,151 --> 00:00:40,388
They can blow up the
damned... dam... for all I care.

12
00:00:40,388 --> 00:00:41,122
Dammit!

13
00:00:41,122 --> 00:00:43,224
[explosions]

14
00:00:43,224 --> 00:00:45,159
I'm pretty sure this is
unconstitutional.

15
00:00:45,159 --> 00:00:47,228
Even cops aren't allowed to mortar people.

16
00:00:47,228 --> 00:00:47,862
I mean, what happened?

17
00:00:47,862 --> 00:00:51,232
Was there an emergency session
of Congress to vote on bombing me?

18
00:00:51,232 --> 00:00:52,500
Okay, think.

19
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,868
I guess I'll just rush them.

20
00:00:53,868 --> 00:00:55,737
If I stagger my approach,
they should miss.

21
00:00:57,972 --> 00:01:00,141
NO!  I CHANGED MY MIND!
I DON'T WANNA DIE!

22
00:01:02,443 --> 00:01:06,681
[underwater panicking]

23
00:01:07,715 --> 00:01:08,616
SHARK!

24
00:01:08,883 --> 00:01:09,884
SHARK!

25
00:01:11,886 --> 00:01:14,088
[underwater panicking]

26
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:18,059
OH MY GOD!  ARE YOU KIDDING ME?!

27
00:01:18,059 --> 00:01:19,427
[gibbering]

28
00:01:19,427 --> 00:01:21,729
I FEEL SUFFICIENTLY MOTIVATED
TO LEAVE THIS PLACE!

29
00:01:21,729 --> 00:01:23,398
I DON'T NEED YOUR ENCOURAGEMENT!

30
00:01:25,199 --> 00:01:26,901
I SAID I DON'T NEED YOUR HELP!

31
00:01:26,901 --> 00:01:29,070
YOU HAVE NO FAITH IN PEOPLE!

32
00:01:29,070 --> 00:01:29,737
[screams]

33
00:01:29,737 --> 00:01:30,638
[panicking]

34
00:01:30,638 --> 00:01:32,974
BOMBS BAD BOMBS BAD BAD BOMBS BAD!

35
00:01:32,974 --> 00:01:35,009
Okay!  Suppressive fire in,
suppressive fire out!

36
00:01:35,009 --> 00:01:37,211
Do the hokey-pokey and
that's what it's all about!

37
00:01:38,179 --> 00:01:39,547
STOP SHOOTING ME!

38
00:01:39,547 --> 00:01:40,848
I'M NOT THE ENEMY!

39
00:01:40,848 --> 00:01:43,551
GET YOUR HEAD OUT OF THE CLOUDS!

40
00:01:48,823 --> 00:01:53,027
Boy... what's it take to get some
peace and quiet around here?

41
00:01:53,027 --> 00:01:55,763
So... let's assess the situation.

42
00:01:55,763 --> 00:01:57,765
I'm in a damned canyon.

43
00:01:57,765 --> 00:02:00,001
I'm stuck on this damned tower.

44
00:02:00,001 --> 00:02:01,970
What's in this damned room anyway?

45
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:04,038
It's a damned button.

46
00:02:04,038 --> 00:02:05,373
[machine powers down]

47
00:02:05,373 --> 00:02:07,675
Sounds like that did some damned thing.

48
00:02:07,675 --> 00:02:09,477
So, how am I going to get out of here?

49
00:02:09,477 --> 00:02:11,846
The soldiers blew up the damned bridge,

50
00:02:11,846 --> 00:02:14,015
and that damned shark's
still in the dammed water.

51
00:02:14,849 --> 00:02:15,984
Ah hah!

52
00:02:21,155 --> 00:02:22,523
Maybe he's faking it.

53
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,495
No, I think I got him.

54
00:02:27,495 --> 00:02:29,831
Well, that's one less damned
problem to worry about.

55
00:02:30,498 --> 00:02:32,800
But, how am I going to get up
these damned walls?

56
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,802
I don't see a damned ladder anywhere.

57
00:02:34,802 --> 00:02:36,504
There's no damned steps.

58
00:02:36,504 --> 00:02:37,905
This is a damned mess.

59
00:02:37,905 --> 00:02:40,408
Why did those damned soldiers
blow that up, anyway?

60
00:02:40,408 --> 00:02:42,243
I bet they're trying to cut
the damned power.

61
00:02:42,243 --> 00:02:46,080
That means, all those scientists are going
to get stuck underground in the dark.

62
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,815
Well, that's their damned problem.

63
00:02:47,815 --> 00:02:50,985
Okay, my options look pretty
damned limited this way.

64
00:02:50,985 --> 00:02:51,819
Ehh...

65
00:02:51,819 --> 00:02:54,088
I'll guess I'll just check out
what's around that bend.

66
00:02:54,088 --> 00:02:57,025
Maybe there's a cruise ship
that'll serve me some drinks.

67
00:02:59,627 --> 00:03:03,831
[underwater mumbling]

68
00:03:04,465 --> 00:03:05,700
Okay...

69
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:07,535
Hey!  There's nothing there at all!

70
00:03:07,535 --> 00:03:09,270
It's a damned dead end!

71
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:10,338
[underwater mumbling]

72
00:03:10,905 --> 00:03:12,907
The water must be seeping in underground.

73
00:03:12,907 --> 00:03:14,742
That doesn't help me at all!

74
00:03:14,742 --> 00:03:16,210
[growling]

75
00:03:17,478 --> 00:03:19,847
I'm sick of this damned place!

76
00:03:19,847 --> 00:03:21,883
I didn't kill that fish just so I could--

77
00:03:23,651 --> 00:03:26,287
--just so I could take over its job!

78
00:03:26,287 --> 00:03:26,921
Hey...

79
00:03:27,388 --> 00:03:28,222
maybe...

80
00:03:28,656 --> 00:03:29,791
...there's a tunnel.

81
00:03:32,026 --> 00:03:33,094
[underwater "Ah hah!"]

82
00:03:34,962 --> 00:03:41,102
[underwater mumbling]

83
00:03:41,102 --> 00:03:45,339
[gasping]

84
00:03:45,339 --> 00:03:47,308
There's some sort of valve down there.

85
00:03:47,308 --> 00:03:50,678
Maybe I could flood the whole canyon.
That'll at least make me feel better.

86
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:02,156
[underwater mumbling]

87
00:04:02,156 --> 00:04:04,225
[gasping]

88
00:04:04,225 --> 00:04:05,526
Okay, we can do this.

89
00:04:05,526 --> 00:04:07,328
Air...air is for losers.

90
00:04:11,599 --> 00:04:14,001
[metal groaning]

91
00:04:14,001 --> 00:04:15,903
[underwater grunting]

92
00:04:15,903 --> 00:04:20,608
[underwater panicking]

93
00:04:20,608 --> 00:04:26,280
[gasping]

94
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:27,348
Haaaa....

95
00:04:27,348 --> 00:04:29,016
Waaaahh.. gaaahhh...

96
00:04:29,016 --> 00:04:33,454
[gasping]

97
00:04:33,454 --> 00:04:34,722
Well...

98
00:04:34,722 --> 00:04:36,257
I'll be damned.

99
00:04:36,257 --> 00:04:39,093
I didn't really think I was going
to do anything like that again.

100
00:04:39,093 --> 00:04:40,528
Okay, let's get down to business.

101
00:04:40,528 --> 00:04:42,096
Does this guy have any money on him?

102
00:04:42,096 --> 00:04:43,164
Or snacks?

103
00:04:44,265 --> 00:04:46,000
This guy doesn't have anything.

104
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,636
Well, don't expect any
fare for Charon from me.

105
00:04:48,636 --> 00:04:51,005
If you're too cheap to keep even
fifty cents in your pocket

106
00:04:51,005 --> 00:04:53,007
before throwing yourself off a dam.

107
00:04:53,007 --> 00:04:54,942
Gotta save your money, right?

108
00:04:55,943 --> 00:04:58,279
This stream better go somewhere.

109
00:04:58,279 --> 00:05:00,481
If it doesn't, I'm going to
have to start an avalanche.

110
00:05:00,481 --> 00:05:02,750
I have explosives.

111
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:05,219
Okay, big giant wall with no steps.

112
00:05:05,219 --> 00:05:06,954
Not what I want to see.

113
00:05:06,954 --> 00:05:08,055
No...

114
00:05:08,689 --> 00:05:09,557
No...!

115
00:05:11,325 --> 00:05:15,029
[growling]

116
00:05:15,029 --> 00:05:16,230
Why lock that gate?

117
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:18,132
Who do they think is going to break in?

118
00:05:18,132 --> 00:05:19,967
I'm trying to break OUT.

119
00:05:19,967 --> 00:05:23,337
They think someone's going to sneak in
with a bucket and steal their water?

120
00:05:23,337 --> 00:05:24,772
Ah.

121
00:05:24,772 --> 00:05:27,141
I could fit into one of these pipes.

122
00:05:27,141 --> 00:05:28,709
But, which one?

123
00:05:28,709 --> 00:05:29,410
I'll try this one.

124
00:05:29,410 --> 00:05:32,880
If there's a midget squatting here with
a knife then I'll just go in the other one.

125
00:05:33,347 --> 00:05:34,015
Hm.

126
00:05:35,149 --> 00:05:37,718
Oh, what the hell?
They tricked me AGAIN!

127
00:05:37,718 --> 00:05:42,256
Why have two runoff pipes if the circumference
is exactly the same as the source?

128
00:05:42,256 --> 00:05:44,158
Although, I like how they
added lights here.

129
00:05:44,158 --> 00:05:47,261
That's awfully considerate --and
wasteful-- of them.

130
00:05:47,261 --> 00:05:50,832
I bet maybe someone comes
through here twice a year.  If that.

131
00:05:50,832 --> 00:05:52,800
But, then again, we have a dam.

132
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,436
May as well pimp the tunnels
with extra electricity.

133
00:05:55,436 --> 00:05:56,370
[helicopter blades whirring, mortar fire]
Oh, no...

134
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:57,905
There's another one?!

135
00:05:58,906 --> 00:06:01,275
Oh, this is going to be a long day.

136
00:06:03,978 --> 00:06:06,180
I'd say I need a surface-to-air missile,

137
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:09,250
but no one should NEED a
surface-to-air missile.

138
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:11,789
That should be firmly under
"Wants and Desires."

139
00:06:11,789 --> 00:06:12,934
This is bullshit.

